#AREA City of Eternity~
#AUTHORS Mazrim ~





#HELPS
-1 CITYETERNITY 'CITY OF ETERNITY'~
CITY OF ETERNITY
The City of Eternity, unlike the Magic Zone, is almost purely my work. When I
say this, I mean that I borrowed very little from books and/or movies. In any
case, there are few, if any references to Robert Jordan, David Eddings,
L.E. Modesitt, or Mercedes Lackey (there is one reference to her Valdemar
books). But they still rock. *grin* I hope that you enjoy the area!

   - Mazrim Taim, M'Hael -<R.K. SUBANG>-

   Sorry. Felt I needed a signature. Subang forever. *grin*

   Revised by Emperor on July 2nd, 1998 and September 27th, 1998.


		(A) The Story 
		(-) Back


{a}CITYETERNITY1
~
-1 CITYETERNITY1~
THE STORY
In times long past, there was a rather ordinary looking crossroads. Just your
average, everyday dusty crossing. Then, late one misty night, just as the moon
reached its peak in the star-dusted sky, thin tendrils of energy began to 
appear. They reached out, and tapped into long-buried ley lines. The power 
began to flow back to the strange, wierd light that began to glow in the night.

Suddenly, the light stretched, becoming a fifteen foot high slash in the very
fabric in time and space. A lone figure hurtled through the dimensional rift,
bolts of some energy unknown to this world flew after him, turning some of the
nearby rocks to slag. The figure leapt to its feet and spun around to face the
rift. He (for the figure was a male of some race) began to intone a spell in
a sonorous voice. The rift began to close rapidly. One of the things that had
been pursuing the man lunged at its intended victim. The rift closed on
the thing, slicing it in half. Even the intense crackling of mage-energies
was drowned out by the shriek of pain, rage and despair of the thing. As
the journeyman mage who had been sleeping nearby looked on in horrified
awe, the figure raised his hand, unleashing a massive blast of power upon
his enemy. The young mage started to back away, falling on his backside in
the process.

He knew only one thing. That power had *not* been any sort of magic.
The newcomer spun around and spotted the young journeyman, who had a very
frightened look on his face. The man began to howl with laughter. "What's so
damned funny?!", the mage spluttered furiously. The man replied, "The look on
your face! And it's just my luck...the first blind rift I make in over a 
milleniium, and I land on my face in front of a mage..." The mage now saw
the man's face clearly. He was definitely human, but he had the face of a 
young man, with eyes that looked like they held the wisdom of the ages. 

As the man looked at the mage curiously, he asked, "What are you doing in
the middle of nowhere at this time of night, anyways?" "I'm seeking my
fortune." "A noble goal, my young friend," replied the fellow. With a
thoughtful look, he said, "May I come with you? I seek knowledge in all
its forms...and I'm pretty good in a fight." Thus, the partnership between
a mage known as the traveller known as Hunter came into being. Eventually
they founded this great city, which even to this day sits upon a lake.

Once the city and its many protections, mundane and magical, were in
place, Lord Hunter left to build his Tower, where to this day, he works on
many wonderful and amazing things.

     (-) Back

{-} CITYETERNITY
~
