>all_greet_prog 100~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 0
 tell $n The name's James. Sir James.
 tell $n Pardon me, but I could use some help...
else
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 2
 tell $n Hi $n
 tell $n I hope your quest to fix the sundial is going ok
else
endif
endif
~
>speech_prog help~
if quest(0, 4, $n) > 0
else
 say Well, my sundial seems to be having a bit of trouble.  
 say Some of the 'special features' aren't working *quite* right.
 say Would you be so good as to take it to my friend for me?  
 say I need it fixed and Sir Hugh is really quite good with gadgets.
 mpmset $n quest 0 4 1
endif
~
>speech_prog p special features~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 1
 mpecho $I waves his hand in the air vaguely.
 say Oh, the options are just little things that I use 
 say from time to time in my line of work, that's all.
 grin $n
 say So will you help then?
else
endif
~
>speech_prog yes~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 1
  if hasobjnum(27390)
     mpquiet on 
     remove sundial
     cast 'giant strength' $n
     mpquiet off
     say Excellent!
     give I27390 $n
  else
     say Excellent!
     say Now, where *did* I put that blasted thing?
     say Ah yes, now I remember!
     mpecho $I pulls a sundial out of his pocket.
     mpoload 27390
     mpquiet on
     cast 'giant strength' $n
     mpquiet off
     give I27390 $n
  endif
 say Oh yes, I almost forgot...  
 say Take this parchment and use it to get into Hugh's Workshop.
 say It's hidden of course... just look for the portal.
 say Oh, by the way, should you lose this thing
 say just come to me, and say 'parchment'.
 say Thanks!
 mpoload 27392
 give I27392 $n
 mpmset $n quest 0 4 2
endif
~
>speech_prog parchment~
if quest (0,4,$n) >= 2
  nod $n
  say Here you go.
  mpoload 27392
  mpquiet on
  cast 'giant strength' $n
  mpquiet off
  give I27392 $n
endif
~
>give_prog I27391~
if quest (0,4,$n) == 3
  nod $n
  tell $n Thank you so very much.  
  tell $n I appreciate your helping me out.
  tell $n Hmm... Would you be interested in some extra work?
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 4
  mpjunk I27391
endif
~
>speech_prog p more careful~
if quest (0,4,$n) >= 3
  mpecho $I looks slightly embarrased.
  tell $n I try to follow his advice.
  tell $n My line of work can be a bit rough though.
  smile
endif
~
>speech_prog work~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 4
  tell $n Well, you have been quite a help...  
  tell $n There's this secret ledger that I really need...
  tell $n If you can get it for me, I'll make it worth your while.
  tell $n If you are interested, just say: 'I will do it!'
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 5
endif
~
>speech_prog p I will do it!~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 5
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 6
  nod $n
  tell $n OK! Now, the reason I need your help 
  tell $n is because I can't get near the place 
  tell $n of the fellow who has the ledger
  tell $n There's just too many people there watching for me
  tell $n However, *you* could probably slip past without difficulty
else
endif
~
>speech_prog difficulty~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 6
  tell $n The person to look for goes by the name: Lethalis Darkmaster.
  tell $n Darkmaster operates a rather seedy pub... 
  tell $n Go to the back of the pub and sneak into the cellar.
  tell $n There's a mercenary guard there...  
else
endif
~
>speech_prog guard~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 6
  tell $n The guard *might* let you by if you ask about the cellar.
  tell $n I wouldn't try him unless the Lord Hunter himself was with me.
  tell $n Nonetheless, he's located in the cellar...
else
endif
~
>speech_prog cellar~
if quest (0,4,$n) == 6
  tell $n The cellar is a storage place for ale and beer 
  tell $n It's not exactly what you would call high quality. 
  tell $n Actually, I've tasted better wet socks and horse piss.
  snicker
  tell $n Anyways, you are looking for some sort of hidden entrance...  
else
endif
~
>speech_prog entrance~
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 6
  tell $n Be cautioned though. There are guards on the other side.  
  tell $n Once you are past the guards, go up into the office.
  tell $n Search his desk for the hidden ledger and bring it to me
  tell $n Oh yeah, that reminds me, I almost forgot...
else
endif
~
>speech_prog forgot~ 
if quest (0, 4, $n) == 6
  tell $n Before you do anything more, go see Hugh
  tell $n Tell him that you need some 'help'.  
  tell $n He'll provide you with something 
  tell $n you'll need for the task.
  tell $n Anyways, once you have the ledger,
  tell $n bring it back to me for your reward.
  tell $n Good luck!
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 7
endif
~
>give_prog I27402~
if quest (0,4,$n) == 7
  gasp $n
  say Dear Order, you've managed to get it!
  say Thank you ever so much!  Here, take this for your help.
  say It may prove useful in the future.
  mpoload 27410
  mpmset $n quest 0 4 8
  mpquiet on
  cast 'giant strength' $n
  mpquiet off
  give I27410 $n
  tell $n Thanks again!
else
endif
~
|
#27383
mercenary guard~
The Mercenary Guard~
A Mercenary Guard stands here, ready for a fight.~
When you were growing up, you heard fantastic stories of mercenary fighters 
who could make the most hardened fighter turn tail by looking at him 
cross-eyed.  But you never believed them. Until now. You wonder if he
may be persuaded to let you into the CELLAR.~
ACT_NO_ORDER|ACT_BODY|ACT_RACE|ACT_SENTINEL|ACT_SMART
AFF_DETECT_INVIS|AFF_DETECT_HIDDEN|AFF_INFRARED|AFF_SANCTUARY
0 S
130 BODY_ARM|BODY_LEG BODY_ARM|BODY_LEG 1d1+26999 1d1+139
100000 RACE_HUMAN
POS_STANDING POS_STANDING SEX_MALE
>all_greet_prog 100~
mpecho $I looks at you coolly, sizing you up.
mpecho $I decides that you are not a threat.
laugh $n
say If you don't make trouble, I won't rearrange your organs.
~
>speech_prog cellar~
mpecho $I looks at you carefully.
say Sure, I can let you in if you make it worth my while...
say As long as I don't let that so-called spy in...
say There's not much in there anyways...  
say Either cough up cash, or find something that I like.
~
>speech_prog p cash~
groan
say What are you, stupid?  Gold.  
say Make it half a mill, and I'll let you in.
~
>bribe_prog 500000~
mpecho $I counts the gold carefully, making sure it's real.
nod
say Ok, very well.  Here you go...
mpecho $I opens the cellar.
mpechoat $n You walk into the cellar.
mpechoaround $n $n walks into the cellar.
mpquiet on
mptransfer $n 27475
mpquiet off
mpecho $I closes the cellar.
~
>give_prog I27377~
mpecho $I looks at the shot carefully.
mpecho $I holds it up to the light.
shrug
mpecho $I slams the shot!
mpjunk I27377
say AH!
